From 9ce93dd7bdac62ab9a150a8f7d69e576271e16b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: equuleus port <port@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] equuleus: point libpn553_fw.so at lib64

The blob list requests vendor/lib/libpn553_fw.so, but the device ships
only vendor/lib64/libpn553_fw.so, and that file is a 64-bit ELF.

Measured on the official LineageOS 22.2 equuleus OTA:
  vendor/lib64/libpn553_fw.so  37490 bytes  ELF64  machine=183 (AArch64)
  vendor/lib/libpn553_fw.so    absent

It is not a loadable shared object: the file has no DT_SONAME and no
DT_NEEDED. It is NXP PN553 NFC firmware in an ELF container, consumed by
name from libnfc-nxp.conf:

  NXP_FW_NAME="libpn553_fw.so"

so no 32-bit ABI is involved. Placing the 64-bit ELF under lib/ to satisfy
the literal path would make a 32-bit consumer fail to map it, which is
worse than a missing file. Correct the path instead.
---
diff --git a/proprietary-files.txt b/proprietary-files.txt
index daa31b0..5be119e 100644
--- a/proprietary-files.txt
+++ b/proprietary-files.txt
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@ vendor/lib64/hw/android.hardware.keymaster@3.0-impl-qti.so
 
 # NFC firmware
 vendor/firmware/libpn553_rec.so
-vendor/lib/libpn553_fw.so
+vendor/lib64/libpn553_fw.so
 
 # QDCM calibration data
 vendor/etc/qdcm_calib_data_ss_notch_fhd_cmd_dsi_panel.xml
-- 
